Usage: gskill search (find) <query> [flags]

Search for skills in a source, a GitHub owner, or configured repositories.

Examples:

    gskill search kubernetes
    gskill search deploy --owner acme
    gskill search deploy --owner gitlab.com/acme/platform
    gskill search deploy --owner bitbucket.org/acme --transport ssh
    gskill search helper --source github.com/owner/repo

Arguments:
  <query>    Keyword to search for (matches name and description).

Flags:
  -h, --help                 Show context-sensitive help.
      --json                 Emit machine-readable JSON on stdout.
      --quiet                Suppress diagnostics on stderr.
      --no-interactive       Disable prompts and colored output.
      --yes                  Assume yes for confirmation prompts.
      --offline              Operate without network access.
      --no-cache             Bypass the content cache.
      --dry-run              Report actions without applying them.
      --config=STRING        Path to a TOML config file; overrides the user
                             config file. Must exist.
  -v, --verbose              Enable verbose diagnostics.
  -C, --dir=STRING           Run as if gskill started in this directory.

      --source=STRING        Search within one source.
      --owner=STRING         Search a GitHub user or organization
                             (acme or github.com/acme), a GitLab group
                             (gitlab.com/acme/platform), or a Bitbucket
                             workspace (bitbucket.org/acme).
      --transport="https"    Clone address used for repositories found with
                             --owner: https or ssh.
